//? Title: Lexicographic breadth-first search
//? Subtitle: Actual ordered partitions, the original seven-vertex graph and elimination witnesses
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Lex-BFS refines an ordered partition after each selected vertex, prioritizing
earlier adjacency distinctions. This report exposes the actual native partitions
and classification decisions, retains the original seven-vertex example and
checks the reversed order as a perfect-elimination candidate. The dense
implementation performs quadratic scans; the linear-time complexity of
specialized Lex-BFS implementations is not claimed for this code.
)

\toc

> Ordered labels without rebuilding the display

Initially every vertex lies in one ordered block[0,...,n−1]. Select the last
member of the first block, remove it, and split each remaining block into its
neighbors followed by its nonneighbors, preserving member order within each
part. Empty parts disappear. The first block represents the largest
adjacency-history label; earlier selected neighbors have priority over later
distinctions. Since members retain ascending order, exact label ties choose the
largest remaining vertex. Thus the initial vertex is n−1, correcting the old
header’s suggestion that selection starts at0.

An equivalent mathematical description gives each unvisited vertex the
decreasing selection numbers of its previously selected neighbors, in
chronological order, and chooses the lexicographically largest list. Partition
splitting implements that label order without explicitly copying labels. It does
not mean that this particular all-block dense scan is a linear-time
implementation.

> A tiny real split

In the four-vertex star with center0, vertex3 is selected first. Its actual
neighbor0 becomes the first block, ahead of nonneighbors1,2. The diagram reads
those actual captured blocks; no report-side refinement replay constructs the
history.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lex_bfs_split.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/lex_bfs.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::lex_bfs_trace(4, {{1, 2, 3}, {0}, {0}, {0}});
    std::print("| actual completed selections | actual selected vertex, initial sentinel minus1 | actual " "remaining ordered blocks |\n| ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t k = 0; k < t.stages.size(); ++k) {
        std::string blocks;
        for (auto &b : t.stages[k].blocks) {
            blocks += "[";
            for (int v : b)
                blocks += std::format("{} ", v);
            blocks += "] ";
        }
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", k, t.stages[k].selected,
                   blocks.empty() ? "empty" : blocks);
    }
    auto &s = t.stages[1];
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("original", {0, 0}, "Actual initial block\n[0,1,2,3]").node(
        "neighbor", {7, 2},
        std::format("Actual selected{}: neighbors\nfirst block[{}]", s.selected,
                    s.blocks[0][0])).node("rest", {7, -2},
                                          std::format("Actual nonneighbors\nnext block[{},{}]",
                                                      s.blocks[1][0],
                                                      s.blocks[1][1])).edge(
        "original", "neighbor").edge("original", "rest").save_svg(
        "build/lex_bfs_split.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| actual completed selections | actual selected vertex, initial sentinel minus1 | actual remaining ordered blocks |
| ---: | ---: | --- |
| 0 | -1 | [0 1 2 3 ]  |
| 1 | 3 | [0 ] [1 2 ]  |
| 2 | 0 | [1 2 ]  |
| 3 | 2 | [1 ]  |
| 4 | 1 | empty |
\image(figures/lex_bfs_split.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual first star-graph split and complete native partition history.)
\alttext(Selecting3 prioritizes its neighbor0; the ordered nonneighbor block preserves1,2, with the final empty partition retained.)

> Original seven-vertex graph

Retain adjacency rows(1,2),(0,2,3),(0,1,3),(1,2,4,5),(3,5),(3,4,6),(5). The
deterministic order is6,5,4,3,2,1,0. The original report computed this order
with the library but separately replayed partition refinement to plot block
counts. The replacement reads the actual producing states and real neighbor
tests. Partition counts can decrease when a singleton block is consumed, so
“ever finer” is not a monotone count claim. The native undirected graph diagram
labels each original identity and its real selection rank.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lex_bfs_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/lex_bfs.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<std::vector<int>> g{{1, 2}, {0, 2, 3}, {0, 1, 3}, {1, 2, 4, 5},
                                    {3, 5}, {3, 4, 6}, {5}};
    auto t = dm::algorithms::lex_bfs_trace(7, g);
    std::print("| actual selection rank | actual selected identity | actual remaining block count |\n| ---: " "| ---: | ---: |\n");
    std::vector<std::size_t> rank(7);
    for (std::size_t k = 0; k < t.analysis.order.size(); ++k) {
        rank[t.analysis.order[k]] = k;
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", k, t.analysis.order[k],
                   t.stages[k + 1].blocks.size());
    }
    std::print("\nActual dense matrix cells {}; actual input entries {}; actual membership tests {}.\n",
               t.analysis.work.matrix_cells, t.analysis.work.adjacency_entries,
               t.analysis.work.neighbor_tests);
    std::vector<dm::geometry::Point2D> positions{{0, 4}, {5, 4}, {0, -2},
                                                 {10, 1}, {15, 4}, {15, -2},
                                                 {20, -2}};
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    for (int v = 0; v < 7; ++v)
        d.node(std::to_string(v), {positions[v].x, positions[v].y},
               std::format("Original vertex{}\nactual rank{}", v, rank[v]));
    for (int u = 0; u < 7; ++u)
        for (int v : g[u])
            if (u < v)
                d.link(std::to_string(u), std::to_string(v));
    d.save_svg("build/lex_bfs_original.svg");
}
```
