\alttext(The native counters show quadratic work despite zero input edges; no linear-time implementation or benchmark timing is claimed.)

> Contracts and verification

Vertex count is nonnegative, adjacency has exactly n rows and every endpoint is
in0..n−1. These complete guards precede matrix allocation. Historical
normalization is explicit: asymmetric entries become undirected edges, duplicate
entries coalesce, loops are ignored, and original rows remain owned in trace.
Ties preserve the old deterministic largest-member choice. Empty and
disconnected graphs are valid. The separate elimination checker requires a full
valid permutation.

The capture admits exactly E+2*n^2+n+1 logical records before copies/evaluation:
E original entries, n^2 matrix cells, n+1 stage records, n*(n+1)/2
remaining-member slots and n*(n−1)/2 actual classifications. It excludes
row/block headers, scalar fields, capacities, result/runtime copies and
bytes/RAM. Default cap is one million;0 disables only that optional cap.
Captures own their data and use one real producer execution.

Native tests exhaust all 1024 five-vertex simple graphs against independent
explicit-label search and brute-force perfect-elimination permutations, and
check normalization, real partitions, counts, witnesses, quotas and ownership.
The ten-report batch passed 101 native CTest cases, 34 directly instrumented
ASan/UBSan cases, 103 compiled/executed public examples, 515/515 scoped file
definitions plus 10 exact LCG class definitions, and ten representative clangd
hovers. Independent Python integer/Fraction, explicit-label graph search,
quadratic sequence DP and full weighted-stump references passed 69430 records
across all ten topics, including a separately fitted held-out Iris model. Frozen
ordinary compatibility passed 1000 Lex-BFS orders, 1000 library sorts, 100 LBG
codebooks, 100 complete five-round LogitBoost ensembles and 200 LLL bases;
corrected LBG final labels/objectives are intentionally excluded from historical
compatibility. All 4 complete programs executed and all 4 native figures were
rendered and visually reviewed, with clipped legends corrected and rerun.
HTML/Markdown computed-result and figure-byte checks gate legacy retirement.
Repeatable receipts are retained in `build/mepml-conversion/batch-204-213/`.

> References

D. J. Rose, R. E. Tarjan and G. S. Lueker(1976),
[Algorithmic Aspects of Vertex Elimination on Graphs|https://doi.org/10.1137/0205021],
SIAM Journal on Computing5(2),266–283. The graph-theoretic relation is retained;
its linear-time implementation bound is explicitly distinguished from this
library’s dense partition scan and separate cubic elimination checker.
